+## 6. Corrections (the PR #733 audit, adjudicated 2026-10-03)
+
+The follow-up audit of PR #733 found this record overclaiming in three
+places and confusing one base commit with another. All four are
+corrected here; the claims as originally written are preserved above
+unchanged, because this file is a record, not a palimpsest.
+
+- **§0 base confusion**: "the series sits on `be8b8569`" was wrong.
+  `be8b8569` is the merge of PR #731 — the base of the *S18 series this
+  document adjudicates*, not of the series that became PR #733. PR #733
+  sits on `27cffb80`, the merge of PR #732 (`36ec052e`, "Harden
+  extraction and close tooling contract gaps"), whose first parent is
+  `be8b8569`. The re-base instruction was honored; the *description* of
+  the base was one merge behind the actual push.
+- **§1 M1 "Closed (undecodable = no semantic evidence …)"**: the
+  undecodable-rendering refusal as shipped in PR #733 was DEFECTIVE, not
+  closed. `_UNDISASM`'s `(?:\(bad\)|\.byte)\b` can never match `(bad)`
+  (``\)'' is a non-word character; `\b` requires a word/non-word
+  transition, and `(bad)` is followed by whitespace or EOL — both
+  non-word), and `semantically_equal` compared `.stdout` without
+  checking `.returncode`, so two FAILED disassemblies compared equal
+  (`"" == ""`) — the exact fail-open this section claimed to have shut.
+  Both corpora did pass, but "verified non-breaking" was true only
+  because nothing in them tripped the holes. The closure is real as of
+  the S14 revision (parser-based, returncode-checked, gap-aware;
+  re-verified below), not as of this record.
+- **§5 "x86-64 asm-diff 1418/0 and i686 672/0 under the pinned pair and
+  the undecodable refusal"**: same defect — those runs were green under
+  the *broken* refusal. The numbers re-verified green under the working
+  one: 1418/0 and 672/0 again (S14 record), so the corpus was never
+  resting on the holes; the claim is now true for the right reason.
+- **Test-count framing**: wherever the delivery described the test
+  outcome as "8 changed-path tests passed, and all other 53 passed"
+  (PR-body phrasing), the arithmetic double-counted: the 8 are a subset
+  of the 53. The accurate statement for PR #733 is **53/55 test_encdiff
+  tests passed, including 8/8 changed-path tests** (the 2 failures were
+  the partial-baseline cases the S14 strict-parse work then made
+  structurally impossible, at 66/66). test_ci_gate_parity was 23/23 and
+  is 24/24 after the lookalike-mutation work.
+
+The review-identifier archaeology this record's series had scattered
+through production comments ("PR #731 audit M2", "S18", "S15", …) is
+swept from the code in the S14 revision; the identifiers remain
+resolvable here and in the S14 record, which carries the mapping.
